hi my name is Serena and I'm going to  tell you about the difference between  the internet and the web as you know one  of the marvels of modern technology is  the internet something you probably use  every day  maybe all day you go on the internet or  you surf the web a lot of people use  these terms the Internet and the web  interchangeably but they actually mean  different things the Internet is the  network of machinery that allows access  to the web the web is just a collection  of pages that may have text or images on  them basically the web is a subset of  Internet traffic to visualize this you  can imagine a highway the physical  highway are the paths between the  computers on the Internet network the  moving vehicles are the packets of  information that travel through these  internet paths there are many types of  vehicles cars trucks and motorcycles  they correspond to the different types  of traffic on the Internet  the cars are analogous to the web  traffic the trucks are to the email  traffic and the motorcycles are to the  media traffic so as you can see there is  a difference between the Internet and  the web being that the Internet contains  the web but the web is not the Internet
 

